efer two materially different readings when the source supports them; one reading plus explicit unresolved questions is acceptable. A formalization describes a named selected control, not whole-bank compliance. Keep fact names, types and definitions stable across comparable alternatives. Formal expressions use parenthesized prefix notation, never Java or Python:\ntrue, false, a declared fact name; (integer 6), (money_hkd 100), (date 2024-11-30);\n(and EXPR EXPR ...), (or EXPR EXPR ...), (not EXPR), (if CONDITION THEN ELSE),\n(= LEFT RIGHT), (> LEFT RIGHT), (>= LEFT RIGHT), (+ LEFT RIGHT), (- LEFT RIGHT).\nDates are Gregorian YYYY-MM-DD, numeric literals are exact integer strings.\nUse the same type on both sides of a comparison. Unknown facts remain unknown.\nscope is Boolean; result has result_type. Never invent a fact's truth value.\nUse null formalization if a requirement cannot be represented in this fragment.\nEvery declared fact needs a meaningful definition, units, source refs and an\nexplicit indication of whether supplying it requires professional judgment. Declare the actual question answered by the result. For Boolean compliance or prohibition decisions begin statement with [TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT] or [TRUE_IS_PROHIBITED] respectively. For a Boolean condition, trigger or eligibility predicate use [TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] and explain precisely what true and false mean. Never relabel a licensing trigger as compliance, prohibition or licence possession. For non-Boolean results use [VALUE] and state the units. These meanings are proposals, not approvals.","method":"Investigate the selected parent using the requested move, uncited source units and supplied counterexamples. Retain justified rival readings and explain any failed hypothesis.","move":"scope-and-definition-distinction","parent":{"assumptions":["The selected control tests applicability of the announced exemption to one corporation, one option transaction and one assessment date.","The explicit commencement date governs the announcement; the promised amendment and gazettal are not treated as unstated conditions precedent.","Product and actor classifications are supplied facts requiring appropriate assessment, not inferred from a product label or the Code's title.","Whether a later notice affects this transaction on the assessment date remains unknown unless supported by further evidence."],"citations":[{"quote":"inform licensed corporations that it will exempt non-centrally cleared single-stock options, equity basket options and equity index options","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u0.0"},{"quote":"from 4 January 2026 until further notice","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u0.0"},{"quote":"licensed corporations’ exposures to non-centrally cleared equity options are currently insignificant","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u1.381"},{"quote":"subject to monitoring and periodic reporting2.","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u3.801"},{"quote":"It implemented an indefinite exemption from the UK bilateral margining requirements for single-stock equity options and index options.","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u4.1019"},{"quote":"Paragraph 7(e) of Part III of Schedule 10 to the Code of Conduct will be amended accordingly and gazetted in due course.","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u6.1357"},{"quote":"As set out in Part III of Schedule 10 to the Code of Conduct for Persons Licensed by or Registered with the Securities and Futures Commission (Code of Conduct).","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u15.1671"}],"distinction":"This reading gives the expressly announced date independent effect while retaining the future-notice limitation. It does not import EU reporting conditions, UK permanence or an exposure threshold. A gazettal-dependent alternative would materially postpone eligibility, but the supplied text does not sufficiently support formalizing that alternative. The strongest uncertainty is the legal implementation and detailed scope supplied by the missing Code and later instruments.","family":"exceptions","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The assessed corporation is a licensed corporation addressed by the SFC circular.","name":"is_licensed_corporation","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d802c45a4262c.u0.0"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed margin obligation for this corporation and transaction would fall within Part III of Schedule 10 absent this announced exemption, taking other applicable scope conditions into account.","name":"otherwise_within_margin_requirements","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d802c45a4262c.u15.1671"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed option transaction is not centrally cleared.","name":"is_non_centrally_cleared","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d802c45a4262c.u0.0"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed instrument is a single-stock option, equity basket option or equity index option within the circular's listed categories.","name":"is_listed_equity_option","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d802c45a4262c.u0.0"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The date for which applicability of the announced exemption is assessed.","name":"assessment_date","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["d802c45a4262c.u0.0"],"type":"date","unit":"Gregorian calendar date"},{"meaning":"On the assessment date, no subsequent SFC notice has become effective that ends or displaces the announced exemption for this assessed transaction. Absence of such a notice from this packet does not establish this fact.","name":"announcement_remains_applicable","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d802c45a4262c.u0.0"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"(and is_non_centrally_cleared is_listed_equity_option (>= assessment_date (date 2026-01-04)) announcement_remains_applicable)","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_licensed_corporation otherwise_within_margin_requirements)"},"local_id":"reading_1","questions":["Do the underlying Code or implementing instruments narrow any listed product category or actor classification?","How does any later notice apply to existing transactions, new transactions and accrued margin obligations?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] For a licensed corporation and an otherwise applicable margin obligation within Part III of Schedule 10, true means the assessed transaction satisfies the proposed conditions for the announced SFC exemption: it is a non-centrally cleared single-stock, equity basket or equity index option, the assessment date is on or after 4 January 2026, and the announcement remains applicable on that date. False means at least one of those conditions fails; it does not establish that margin is owed under every other rule. Outside the stated scope this control supplies no applicability decision, and unknown facts remain unknown.","subject":"Applicability of the announced SFC equity-option margin exemption"},"protocol":"legalmath.search.v1","role":"adversarial-investigator","source_packet":{"authority":"RETAINED_SOURCE","dependencies":[{"dependency_id":"missing.60583204ae3dc30d17bad37f","source_hash":null},{"dependency_id":"missing.3fa08e37cc9ca8964c94abb9","source_hash":null},{"dependency_id":"missing.4dd72c04a8ea00444bb6b1a9","source_hash":null}],"family_ids":["scope","definitions","exceptions","modality","time","dependencies"],"selected_slice":"Applicability of the announced SFC margin exemption from 4 January 2026 for classified licensed corporations and non-centrally cleared single-stock, equity-basket or equity-index options. Preserve until-further-notice temporal limitation, pending Code amendment, and the distinction between SFC operative scope and overseas explanatory background.","source_key":"assurance.387982acc9842136e9fa9d1e","units":[{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=25EC71 chars 0:379","normative":true,"span":{"end":379,"id":"s.d802c45a4262c.u0.0","page":1,"quote_sha256":"a36633150fcffe60a071c6896ab4a5fc2b0768be6c8f31d18d5fd0c0101c5a2e","raw_sha256":"1dedb0b381106d5b0d91450c6e99e7da3b96e9646710c502a67263301da99d79","source_id":"d802c45a4262c","start":0,"text_sha256":"569f398a4c60995653627478e273846ebe2d39e6742c7e485a4e1e2ad41859df"},"text":"The Securities and Futures Commission (SFC) issues this circular to inform licensed corporations that it will exempt non-centrally cleared single-stock options, equity basket options and equity index options (collectively, “non-centrally cleared equity options”) from its margin requirements1 from 4 January 2026 until further notice to align with the latest global developments.","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u0.0"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=25EC71 chars 381:794","normative":true,"span":{"end":794,"id":"s.d802c45a4262c.u1.381","page":1,"quote_sha256":"033ae5b076cb4ff461c896eadbe658b0bb503320092dd50db903844a32423fe5","raw_sha256":"1dedb0b381106d5b0d91450c6e99e7da3b96e9646710c502a67263301da99d79","source_id":"d802c45a4262c","start":381,"text_sha256":"569f398a4c60995653627478e273846ebe2d39e6742c7e485a4e1e2ad41859df"},"text":"The margin requirements for non-centrally cleared equity options were originally scheduled to take effect on that date. However, to prevent regulatory arbitrage and considering that licensed corporations’ exposures to non-centrally cleared equity options are currently insignificant, the SFC has decided to align the exemptions of its margin requirements with the approaches in the European Union (EU) and the UK:","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u1.381"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=25EC71 chars 801:1015","normative":true,"span":{"end":1015,"id":"s.d802c45a4262c.u3.801","page":1,"quote_sha256":"c069f0ab4afee3e1f01784867ad9882a0414166313441f2fbae81e2355e2050a","raw_sha256":"1dedb0b381106d5b0d91450c6e99e7da3b96e9646710c502a67263301da99d79","source_id":"d802c45a4262c","start":801,"text_sha256":"569f398a4c60995653627478e273846ebe2d39e6742c7e485a4e1e2ad41859df"},"text":"In the EU, a permanent exemption from the requirement to exchange margin for single-stock equity options and equity index options became effective on 24 December 2024, subject to monitoring and periodic reporting2.","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u3.801"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=25EC71 chars 1019:1352","normative":true,"span":{"end":1352,"id":"s.d802c45a4262c.u4.1019","page":1,"quote_sha256":"12a83cf473c3de087b31245c9823ea224829441891ae78f07a747a61c75a0a09","raw_sha256":"1dedb0b381106d5b0d91450c6e99e7da3b96e9646710c502a67263301da99d79","source_id":"d802c45a4262c","start":1019,"text_sha256":"569f398a4c60995653627478e273846ebe2d39e6742c7e485a4e1e2ad41859df"},"text":"On 27 November 2025, the UK’s Prudential Regulation Authority and Financial Conduct Authority published a joint policy statement3 containing amendments to the Binding Technical Standards 2016/22514. It implemented an indefinite exemption from the UK bilateral margining requirements for single-stock equity options and index options.","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u4.1019"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=25EC71 chars 1357:1477","normative":true,"span":{"end":1477,"id":"s.d802c45a4262c.u6.1357","page":1,"quote_sha256":"635f222ca87a5a684ee7574336a7962912f83261c14e87364e7198269c3e4837","raw_sha256":"1dedb0b381106d5b0d91450c6e99e7da3b96e9646710c502a67263301da99d79","source_id":"d802c45a4262c","start":1357,"text_sha256":"569f398a4c60995653627478e273846ebe2d39e6742c7e485a4e1e2ad41859df"},"text":"Paragraph 7(e) of Part III of Schedule 10 to the Code of Conduct will be amended accordingly and gazetted in due course.","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u6.1357"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=25EC71 chars 1479:1581","normative":true,"span":{"end":1581,"id":"s.d802c45a4262c.u7.1479","page":1,"quote_sha256":"000f162baa0064ac9b13c7642e1d018e4c92362539df6a24578dfec418ad032a","raw_sha256":"1dedb0b381106d5b0d91450c6e99e7da3b96e9646710c502a67263301da99d79","source_id":"d802c45a4262c","start":1479,"text_sha256":"569f398a4c60995653627478e273846ebe2d39e6742c7e485a4e1e2ad41859df"},"text":"Should you have any queries regarding the contents of this circular, please contact your case officer.","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u7.1479"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=25EC71 chars 1587:1610","normative":true,"span":{"end":1610,"id":"s.d802c45a4262c.u10.1587","page":1,"quote_sha256":"9b5b81506e6b64492c143b14fff4eeee4d17eef11e4a9aa5275b47e35195e2f2","raw_sha256":"1dedb0b381106d5b0d91450c6e99e7da3b96e9646710c502a67263301da99d79","source_id":"d802c45a4262c","start":1587,"text_sha256":"569f398a4c60995653627478e273846ebe2d39e6742c7e485a4e1e2ad41859df"},"text":"Intermediaries Division","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u10.1587"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=25EC71 chars 1614:1647","normative":true,"span":{"end":1647,"id":"s.d802c45a4262c.u12.1614","page":1,"quote_sha256":"88e2bc94e9edc39f2ac1cdaaea86b44ab5ea59b31c446f69591f21bf460b005e","raw_sha256":"1dedb0b381106d5b0d91450c6e99e7da3b96e9646710c502a67263301da99d79","source_id":"d802c45a4262c","start":1614,"text_sha256":"569f398a4c60995653627478e273846ebe2d39e6742c7e485a4e1e2ad41859df"},"text":"Securities and Futures Commission","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u12.1614"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=25EC71 chars 1649:1652","normative":true,"span":{"end":1652,"id":"s.d802c45a4262c.u13.1649","page":1,"quote_sha256":"f4db1e48476f60753980b10d66219042b3a3d9c65c9cc77a53d81b88fd869c64","raw_sha256":"1dedb0b381106d5b0d91450c6e99e7da3b96e9646710c502a67263301da99d79","source_id":"d802c45a4262c","start":1649,"text_sha256":"569f398a4c60995653627478e273846ebe2d39e6742c7e485a4e1e2ad41859df"},"text":"End","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u13.1649"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/cir